{#
  One calendar's row on Configuration > Calendrier — the SAME card for a
  section calendar and a supplementary one, which is the whole point of
  this partial: the two lists used to hand-roll their own layout, so the
  identical pair of permission selects sat on one line here and on
  another line there, and neither survived a phone screen (two selects
  capped at 200/230px squeezed onto one non-wrapping flex row next to the
  name).

  The pair now sits in a grid that stacks on mobile and pairs up from
  `sm` on, each select carrying a visible label — « Vu par » /
  « Modifié par » — instead of relying on the option text to explain
  itself. Those two words are all the room a phone has, and a dozen
  calendars down the page would otherwise give a screen reader a dozen
  identically-named controls, so the accessible name adds the calendar's
  own name after them (`label_suffix`, hidden inside the label itself —
  « Vu par » on screen, « Vu par — Meute » to a screen reader): it starts
  with what is written on screen, which is what keeps voice control
  working (WCAG 2.5.3).

  Params:
    calendar_id      -- int, the row's calendar
    name             -- string, displayed name
    color            -- string|null, the section's colour dot (sections only)
    badges           -- string[], optional badges after the name
    visibility       -- 'public'|'chief'|'admin'
    edit_role_min    -- 'chief'|'admin'
    edit_chief_label -- the wording of the 'chief' option ("ses animateurs"
                        on a section calendar, "les animateurs" elsewhere)

  Block `extra` -- filled through {% embed %} by the supplementary list
  (its ICS link block and its Régénérer/Supprimer buttons), empty for a
  section calendar, which has no individual ICS link of its own.
#}
<div class="border rounded-3 p-3" data-calendar-id="{{ calendar_id }}">
    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2 flex-wrap mb-2">
        {% if color|default(null) %}
            <span class="d-inline-block rounded-circle flex-shrink-0" style="width:0.7rem;height:0.7rem;background-color:{{ color }};"></span>
        {% endif %}
        <span class="fw-semibold">{{ name }}</span>
        {% for badge in badges|default([]) %}
            <span class="badge text-bg-secondary">{{ badge }}</span>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <div class="row g-2">
        <div class="col-12 col-sm-6">
            {% include 'partials/form_field.html.twig' with {
                field_id: 'calendar-visibility-' ~ calendar_id,
                label: 'Vu par', type: 'select', size: 'sm', wrapper_class: '',
                control_class_extra: 'visibility-select',
                data: { 'calendar-id': calendar_id },
                label_suffix: ' — ' ~ name,
                options: [
                    { value: 'public', label: 'Tous', selected: visibility == 'public' },
                    { value: 'chief', label: 'Les animateurs', selected: visibility == 'chief' },
                    { value: 'admin', label: "Les chefs d'unité", selected: visibility == 'admin' },
                ],
            } only %}
        </div>
        <div class="col-12 col-sm-6">
            {% include 'partials/form_field.html.twig' with {
                field_id: 'calendar-edit-role-' ~ calendar_id,
                label: 'Modifié par', type: 'select', size: 'sm', wrapper_class: '',
                control_class_extra: 'edit-role-select',
                data: { 'calendar-id': calendar_id },
                label_suffix: ' — ' ~ name,
                options: [
                    { value: 'chief', label: edit_chief_label, selected: edit_role_min == 'chief' },
                    { value: 'admin', label: "Les chefs d'unité", selected: edit_role_min == 'admin' },
                ],
            } only %}
        </div>
    </div>
    {% block extra %}{% endblock %}
</div>
